---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Accessibility · Niko"
  description="How Niko apps are built and tested for accessibility, what is known not to work yet, and how to report a problem."
>
  <nav class="crumb"><a href="/">Niko</a> / Accessibility</nav>
  <header class="hero">
    <h1>Accessibility</h1>
    <p class="lead">Niko apps are made for people mainstream apps leave out. This page says what we do, what we have tested, and what we haven't yet.</p>
  </header>

  <main id="main">
    <section aria-labelledby="built">
      <h2 id="built">How the apps are built</h2>
      <ul class="promise">
        <li><strong>Spoken.</strong> Apps speak in the phone's own voice, in the person's language, so they can be used without reading.</li>
        <li><strong>Labelled.</strong> Every button and setting has a label for TalkBack.</li>
        <li><strong>Large.</strong> Touch targets are at least 64dp, main buttons at least 96dp. Text follows the phone's font size and is designed to work at 200%.</li>
        <li><strong>High contrast.</strong> Colours are chosen for a 7:1 contrast ratio in light and dark themes.</li>
        <li><strong>Calm.</strong> The main screen never scrolls or rearranges, so people can learn where things are.</li>
        <li><strong>Checked on every build.</strong> Android's accessibility checks run on every build and stop it if they fail.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="tested">
      <h2 id="tested">What has been tested</h2>
      <p><strong>Niko Clock 0.3.0</strong> is a test release. It has been tried by hand on a Xiaomi phone and checked on the Android emulator. It has not yet had:</p>
      <ul class="links">
        <li>a full TalkBack pass of every screen, including setup and the PIN screens</li>
        <li>checks at 200% font size on every screen and widget size</li>
        <li>an Accessibility Scanner pass</li>
        <li>testing with people who can't read, blind people or older people using it every day</li>
        <li>a native speaker review of the Hindi, Spanish and Portuguese phrases</li>
      </ul>
      <p>These come before version 1.0. We don't claim conformance with any standard until it has been tested.</p>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="known">
      <h2 id="known">Known problems</h2>
      <ul class="links">
        <li>The settings gear, back arrow and backspace show only an icon. Each has a TalkBack label.</li>
        <li>On the smallest widget size with very large text, the date can be cut short.</li>
        <li>Some phones stop apps in the background to save battery. The app warns about this and shows how to fix it, but can't always detect the phone maker's own settings.</li>
      </ul>
    </section>

    <section aria-labelledby="report">
      <h2 id="report">Tell us what doesn't work</h2>
      <p>If something is hard to use, we want to know. Email <a href="mailto:hello@gopalkhadka.com.np">hello@gopalkhadka.com.np</a> or <a href="https://github.com/NikoApps/Clock/issues">open an issue on GitHub</a>. A voice message or a few words is enough.</p>
      <p>Niko is a one-person side project. Every message is read, and replies usually come within a week. Last updated 18 October 2026.</p>
    </section>
  </main>
</BaseLayout>
